  conc_curl: ['Biceps are isolated with a strong peak contraction.', 'Sit on a bench with your legs apart and rest the back of your upper arm against your inner thigh.|Hold a dumbbell with your arm hanging straight.|Curl the dumbbell up toward your shoulder.|Lower slowly to a full stretch.', 'Keep the upper arm still against the leg.|Squeeze at the top.', 'Swinging the body.|Rushing the lowering phase.'],
  spider_curl: ['Biceps with a strong contraction at the top, since gravity loads the shortened position.', 'Lie chest-down on an incline bench with your arms hanging straight down holding dumbbells.|Keep your upper arms vertical.|Curl the dumbbells up toward your shoulders.|Lower slowly to straight arms.', 'Keep your chest on the bench.|Squeeze hard at the top.', 'Swinging the elbows back.|Using too much weight.'],
  machine_curl: ['Biceps are isolated, and the machine gives a fixed path and support.', 'Adjust the seat so your upper arms rest on the pad with your shoulders level with the top.|Grip the handles with palms facing up.|Curl the handles toward your shoulders.|Lower slowly to almost straight arms.', 'Keep your armpits on the pad.|Control the way down.', 'Lifting the elbows from the pad.|Letting the weight stack drop.'],
  // ---- triceps ----
  pushdown: ['Triceps are isolated, with all three heads contributing.', 'Set a high pulley with a straight bar or V-bar and stand close.|Grip the bar with elbows pinned at your sides.|Press the bar down until your arms are straight.|Return slowly until your forearms are just past parallel.', 'Keep your elbows tight to your ribs.|Squeeze the triceps at the bottom.', 'Leaning over and pushing with the body.|Letting the elbows flare away from the sides.'],
  oh_ext: ['Triceps with an emphasis on the long head, because the arm is overhead.', 'Set a pulley at a high or mid position and hold the rope facing away from the stack.|Step forward with elbows pointing up beside your head.|Extend your arms forward until they are straight.|Return slowly to a deep stretch behind your head.', 'Keep your elbows close to your head.|Brace your core and avoid arching.', 'Letting the elbows flare wide.|Arching the lower back to push.'],
  skull: ['Triceps with extra long head involvement, since the arms are angled back.', 'Lie on a bench holding an EZ-bar over your chest with an overhand grip.|Keep your upper arms still and bend your elbows.|Lower the bar toward your forehead or just behind it.|Extend your elbows to return to the top.', 'Keep your elbows pointing at the ceiling.|Use a controlled tempo.', 'Letting the elbows flare wide.|Lowering with a fast drop.'],
  cgbp: ['Triceps lead, with chest and front delts assisting.', 'Lie on a bench and grip the bar about shoulder width, narrower than a normal bench press.|Unrack and hold the bar over your chest.|Lower to your lower chest with elbows tucked at about 30 degrees.|Press back up to straight arms.', 'Do not go too narrow, which stresses the wrists.|Keep elbows tight to the body.', 'Gripping the bar too narrow.|Bouncing the bar off the chest.'],
  rope_pd: ['Triceps are isolated, with extra lateral head work from spreading the rope at the bottom.', 'Set a high pulley with a rope and stand close.|Pin your elbows beside your ribs.|Press the rope down and pull the ends apart at the bottom.|Return slowly to just past 90 degrees at the elbow.', 'Spread the rope at the bottom for a stronger squeeze.|Keep your upper arms still.', 'Letting the shoulders rock forward.|Using bodyweight to push the weight down.'],
  db_oh_ext: ['Triceps with the long head emphasised, due to the overhead position.', 'Sit or stand holding one dumbbell with both hands overhead.|Keep your elbows pointing forward.|Lower the weight behind your head by bending the elbows.|Extend your arms back to the top.', 'Keep the upper arms close to your head.|Brace your core.', 'Flaring the elbows out.|Arching the lower back.'],
  kickback: ['Triceps are isolated, with a strong contraction at the end of the movement.', 'Hinge forward with a flat back, one hand on a bench, holding a dumbbell in the other hand with your upper arm tucked to your side.|Keep your upper arm parallel to the floor.|Extend your elbow until your arm is straight.|Return slowly to a 90 degree bend.', 'Keep the upper arm still.|Squeeze at the top.', 'Swinging the dumbbell with momentum.|Dropping the elbow.'],
  rev_pd: ['Triceps with a bias toward the medial head, using a reverse (underhand) grip.', 'Set a high pulley with a single handle and hold it with an underhand grip.|Pin your elbow to your side.|Press the handle down until your arm is straight.|Return slowly with control.', 'Keep your elbow stationary.|Use lighter weight than a normal pushdown.', 'Rotating the torso.|Letting the elbow flare.'],
  machine_dip: ['Triceps lead, with the chest assisting, and the machine controlling the path.', 'Adjust the seat so the handles are at your lower chest when seated.|Hold the handles and sit upright with your back on the pad.|Press the handles down until your arms are straight.|Return slowly to the starting position.', 'Keep your shoulders down.|Move with control.', 'Leaning forward and cheating the movement.|Shrugging at the top.'],
  bench_dip: ['Triceps lead, with front delts assisting.', 'Sit on a bench and place your hands beside your hips with fingers forward.|Slide your hips off the bench and straighten your legs or bend your knees.|Lower your body by bending your elbows to about 90 degrees.|Press back up to straight arms.', 'Keep your back close to the bench.|Do not drop below 90 degrees to protect the shoulders.', 'Letting the shoulders roll forward.|Dropping too deep.'],
  diamond_pu: ['Triceps lead, with the chest and front delts assisting.', 'Get into a push-up position with your hands forming a diamond under your chest.|Brace your core and keep your body straight.|Lower your chest toward your hands.|Press back up to straight arms.', 'Keep your elbows tucked close to the body.|Drop to your knees if needed.', 'Letting the hips sag.|Flaring the elbows out.'],
  // ---- forearms ----
