  rev_wrist: ['Forearm extensors on the top of the forearm.', 'Sit with your forearms resting on your thighs or a bench, palms down, holding light dumbbells.|Let your wrists bend down.|Raise the weights by extending your wrists up.|Lower slowly through the full range.', 'Use a light weight.|Keep your forearms still.', 'Going too heavy.|Using momentum from the arms.'],
  btb_wrist: ['Forearm flexors, with an emphasis on grip strength.', 'Stand holding a barbell behind your back with an overhand or underhand grip and arms straight.|Let the bar roll toward your fingertips.|Curl your wrists up to lift the bar.|Lower slowly with control.', 'Keep your arms still and straight.|Hold the top for a brief moment.', 'Bending the elbows to lift.|Letting the bar slip out of the hands.'],
  rev_curl: ['Forearms (brachioradialis) lead, with the biceps assisting.', 'Stand holding a barbell with an overhand shoulder-width grip.|Keep your elbows beside your ribs.|Curl the bar up to shoulder height.|Lower slowly to straight arms.', 'Keep wrists straight.|Use lighter weight than a normal curl.', 'Letting the wrists bend back.|Swinging the body.'],
  farmer: ['Grip and forearms lead, with the upper back and core stabilising.', 'Pick up a heavy dumbbell in each hand and stand tall.|Keep your shoulders back and core braced.|Walk with short, steady steps for the set time.|Set the weights down under control. Count seconds as reps.', 'Keep your posture tall and shoulders level.|Take small, controlled steps.', 'Leaning to one side.|Rushing with long, uneven steps.'],
  dead_hang: ['Grip and forearms lead, with the lats assisting, and it helps shoulder health.', 'Grip a pull-up bar with an overhand grip a little wider than shoulders.|Hang with arms straight and shoulders relaxed down.|Hold the position for the target time.|Step down carefully. Count seconds as reps.', 'Pull the shoulder blades slightly down.|Breathe steadily.', 'Swinging or twisting.|Shrugging up to the ears.'],
  // ---- core ----
  leg_raise: ['Lower abs and hip flexors lead, with the grip and forearms working to hold on.', 'Hang from a pull-up bar with arms straight and shoulders engaged.|Brace your core and keep your legs together.|Raise your legs until they reach hip height or higher, curling the pelvis up.|Lower slowly without swinging.', 'Tilt the pelvis up at the top, not just the legs.|Keep the movement controlled.', 'Swinging the legs with momentum.|Using only the hip flexors with an arched back.'],
  crunch: ['Upper abs lead, with constant tension from the cable.', 'Kneel below a high pulley holding a rope behind your head.|Keep your hips still.|Curl your ribs toward your pelvis, rounding the spine.|Return slowly to the start without sitting back on your heels.', 'Think of crunching your ribs down to your hips.|Exhale as you crunch.', 'Pulling with the arms or hips instead of the abs.|Sitting back with every rep.'],
  plank: ['The whole abdominal wall works to resist sagging, with glutes and shoulders helping.', 'Place your forearms on the floor with elbows under your shoulders.|Extend your legs and lift your body into a straight line.|Brace your abs and squeeze your glutes.|Hold for the target time. Count seconds as reps.', 'Tuck your pelvis slightly.|Breathe steadily.', 'Letting the hips sag or pike up.|Holding your breath.'],
  ab_wheel: ['Abs lead, with lats and shoulders stabilising, and it is a hard anti-extension exercise.', 'Kneel on a mat holding an ab wheel under your shoulders.|Brace your core and tuck your pelvis.|Roll forward until your body is nearly straight without your hips sagging.|Pull the wheel back by bracing your abs.', 'Keep a slight rounded back.|Only go as far as you can control.', 'Letting the lower back arch.|Rolling too far and collapsing.'],
  crunch_bw: ['Upper abs lead.', 'Lie on your back with knees bent and feet flat.|Place your hands across your chest or lightly behind your head.|Curl your shoulders off the floor by bringing your ribs toward your pelvis.|Lower slowly.', 'Do not pull on your neck.|Keep the lower back on the floor.', 'Pulling the head forward with the hands.|Using momentum and sitting all the way up.'],
  bicycle: ['Abs and obliques lead, with hip flexors assisting.', 'Lie on your back with your hands lightly behind your head and legs lifted.|Bring one knee toward your chest while rotating your opposite elbow toward it.|Switch sides in a pedalling motion.|Keep the movement slow and controlled.', 'Rotate from the ribs, not the elbows.|Keep your lower back pressed down.', 'Pulling on the neck.|Rushing the reps.'],
  rev_crunch: ['Lower abs lead.', 'Lie on your back with your legs raised and knees bent to 90 degrees.|Brace your core.|Curl your hips off the floor by bringing your knees toward your chest.|Lower slowly without letting your feet touch.', 'Lift with the abs, not by swinging.|Keep the movement small and controlled.', 'Swinging the legs.|Rolling onto the neck.'],
  side_plank: ['Obliques lead, with glutes and shoulder stabilisers.', 'Lie on your side with your elbow under your shoulder and your legs stacked.|Lift your hips so your body forms a straight line.|Brace your core and hold for the target time.|Switch sides. Count seconds as reps.', 'Keep your hips stacked and lifted.|Breathe steadily.', 'Letting the hips drop.|Rotating the torso forward or back.'],
  russian: ['Obliques lead, with the abs and hip flexors assisting.', 'Sit with knees bent and lean back slightly with your torso at about 45 degrees.|Lift your feet or keep them on the floor.|Rotate your torso side to side, touching the floor or a weight next to your hips.|Keep the movement controlled.', 'Rotate from the ribs.|Keep your chest up.', 'Rounding the back.|Moving only the arms.'],
  knee_raise: ['Lower abs and hip flexors lead.', 'Support yourself on the captain chair with forearms on the pads and back against the pad.|Brace your core.|Raise your knees toward your chest, curling your pelvis up.|Lower slowly without swinging.', 'Curl the pelvis at the top.|Keep your back pressed to the pad.', 'Swinging the legs.|Lowering too fast.'],
  dead_bug: ['Deep abs lead, with an emphasis on core control.', 'Lie on your back with arms straight up and knees bent over your hips.|Press your lower back into the floor.|Lower the opposite arm and leg toward the floor slowly.|Return and switch sides.', 'Keep the lower back pressed down.|Move slowly.', 'Letting the lower back arch.|Moving too fast.'],
  decline_situp: ['Abs lead, with hip flexors assisting.', 'Secure your feet on a decline bench and sit back with arms across your chest.|Brace your core.|Curl your torso up toward your knees.|Lower slowly with control.', 'Curl the spine up instead of swinging.|Keep your chin tucked slightly.', 'Yanking the neck.|Using momentum.'],
  pallof: ['Abs and obliques resist rotation, so the core works as a stabiliser.', 'Set a cable at chest height and stand side-on, holding the handle at your chest.|Step away for tension and brace your core.|Press the handle straight out in front of you.|Hold briefly and return slowly.', 'Do not let the cable rotate your torso.|Keep your hips square.', 'Twisting toward the weight.|Using too heavy a load.'],
  woodchop: ['Obliques lead, with the abs and hips assisting.', 'Set a cable at the high or low position and stand side-on.|Grip the handle with both hands.|Pull the handle diagonally across your body, rotating from the torso.|Return slowly to the start.', 'Pivot the back foot as you rotate.|Keep your arms mostly straight.', 'Rotating only the arms.|Using momentum from the legs.'],
  machine_crunch: ['Abs lead, with the machine giving a fixed resistance.', 'Adjust the seat so the pad rests on your upper chest.|Hold the handles and brace your core.|Crunch forward by bringing your ribs toward your hips.|Return slowly to the start.', 'Round the spine, do not just bend at the hips.|Exhale as you crunch.', 'Using the arms to pull.|Using a weight that is too heavy.'],
  // ---- quads ----
